e-season-final-week","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Montana State ranked No. 1, 5-7 LIU makes FCS bracket as conference champ","description":"Defending national champion Montana State received the top seed for the 24-team FCS playoffs, while Northeast Conference champion LIU (5-7) became the first playoff team with a losing record since 2017.","published":"2026-11-23T00:02:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564910/montana-state-grabs-top-seed-24-team-fcs-playoff-bracket","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest rewards DC Scottie Hazelton with contract extension","description":"Wake Forest defensive coordinator Scottie Hazelton has signed a contract extension.","published":"2026-11-22T21:20:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564902/wake-forest-rewards-dc-scottie-hazelton-extension","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 college football coaching carousel: Tracking every open job","description":"As the carousel spins, we'll keep you updated with all the comings and goings.","published":"2026-11-22T20:32:48.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50358611/2026-cfb-coaching-carousel-firings-hirings","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who are the candidates and what are the priorities after TCU fired Sonny Dykes?","description":"Things started well for Dykes, but now the Horned Frogs are looking for a new coach and should have options.","published":"2026-11-22T19:55:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50323301/tcu-candidates-personnel-recruits","type":"Story","byline":"Eli Lederman, Max Olson and Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What are the conference title game clinching scenarios for Week 12?","description":"Here's what teams from every conference would need to play for their league championship.","published":"2026-11-22T19:15:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50512475/conference-title-game-clinching-scenarios-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"No Big Ten football teams in AP top 5 for first time since 2021","description":"A weekend of Big Ten upsets left the conference without a team in the top five of the AP Top 25 college football poll for the first time since 2021.","published":"2026-11-22T20:22:13.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50563638/no-big-ten-football-teams-ap-top-5-first-21","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4922981/rasheem-biles","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rasheem_Biles"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Rasheem Biles","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rasheem_Biles","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:23Z","intro":"Rasheem Biles (born November 18, 2005) is an American college football linebacker for the Texas Longhorns. He previously played for the Pittsburgh Panthers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Biles attended Pickerington High School Central in Pickerington, Ohio, where he played wide receiver, running back and defensive back. As a senior he played in five games due to injury and had over 400 all-purpose yards and five total touchdowns including two interceptions returned for touchdown. As a junior he had 74 tackles and three interceptions with two returned for a touchdown. Biles committed to the University of Pittsburgh to play college."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"PITTSBURGH\nAs a true freshman at Pittsburgh in 2023, Biles played in nine games and tied a school record with three blocked punts. He became a starter his sophomore year in 2024, starting nine of 12 games and recording 82 tackles, 5.5 sacks and an interception which he returned for a touchdown. He returned to Pittsburgh as a starter in 2025, playing in 10 games and recording 101 tackles, 4.5 sacks, two interceptions, both returned for touchdowns, two forced fumbles, and one fumble recovery, returned for a touchdown. At the end of the season, Biles entered the transfer portal.\n\nTEXAS\nOn January 10, 2026, Biles committed to Texas. In Week 9 against Mississippi State, Biles recorded eight tackles, including three sacks and four tackles for a loss, and two forced fumbles, earning SEC Co-Defensive Player of the Week for his performance."}]}}